[profiles.guide]
notes = '''Hold {select} and {start} together to pause the gyro while you reposition the controller. Press {lb} and {rb} together to switch the gyro off or on, and hold {l3} to recenter it.
{start} (Escape) opens the game's menu and backs out of it. Double tap {start} to quick save (F6) and hold it to quick load (F9).
{rt} attacks; hold it to wind up a power attack, and with a spell readied it casts. {lt} parries with your weapon or shield. {west} kicks: into spikes, off ledges and into fires.
{south} uses, talks, and picks up and carries things; {rt} throws what you carry. Hold {south} to sprint. {east} jumps, and a light push of the left stick {ls} walks quietly. {l3} toggles crouch, for sneaking. {north} uses your special ability once the adrenaline bar is full.
Hold {lb} for the belt ring, aiming with the right stick {rs}: its nine slots hold weapons, spells and potions, which you place there in the inventory. {up} and {down} step through the belt, and {left} and {right} lean. Hold {r3} to zoom while drawing a bow.
{select} (Tab) opens the inventory, and a long press of {select} the objectives (O). In the inventory the right stick moves the pointer and {rt} clicks.
{rb} is free. The Xbox 360 edition (Elements) is a rebuilt game with its own controls, so this scheme is built on the PC keys.
The keys are the game's defaults from a fan-made controls list and not checked in the game (the special ability, bow zoom, walk and quick load especially). Steam and retail copies have been reported to install a French AZERTY keymap; if moving forward is on Z in the game's options, reset the keys to the defaults there. Compare them with Options → Keyboard and change the buttons here to match. The Steam app id is from PCGamingWiki and the executable from Discord's game list; the multiplayer app (2130) isn't matched. The gyro's real-world turn assumes Source's turn of 0.022 degrees a count and a mouse sensitivity of 3, worked out, not measured; set the full turn to 16364 divided by your sensitivity.'''

